pulled out of its resting place by some evil force.
~
1 0 0 S
7 14 3 3d4+90 3d4+0
696 0
0 0 0
>speech_prog hi hello hey greetings yo sup hail howdy~
if rand(25)
mpecho $I says 'Hello yourself. That's the warm part of this conversation over with.'
else
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Greetings, stranger. You'll be a stranger right up until you owe me money or a funeral.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I nods the exact amount of nod required by law and no more.
else
mpecho $I says 'Hi. Yes. Hello. We've done the pleasant part. What do you actually want?'
endif
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog bye later goodbye cya farewell leaving gtg~
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Leaving already? Try to do it in one piece. It's harder than it sounds around here.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'Goodbye. If you come back through still breathing, I'll be mildly impressed.'
else
mpecho $I waves you off with the energy of someone who has waved off a great many people who never returned.
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog thanks thank ty cheers appreciate grateful~
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Thanks don't spend. But I'll allow it, just this once.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'You're welcome. Now go be useful somewhere that isn't directly in front of me.'
else
mpecho $I says 'Gratitude. From an adventurer. I'll have this moment mounted on the wall.'
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog sorry oops apologies mybad pardon~
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Sorry doesn't unbreak the vase, the window, or the previous hero. But noted.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'Apology accepted. Reluctantly. Provisionally. Watch yourself.'
else
mpecho $I says 'Oh, NOW you're sorry. The dramatic timing on you people, I swear.'
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog who name you yourself are~
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Who am I? I'm the one still standing here after watching a hundred of you not.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'My name's my business. Yours is about to be on a gravestone if you keep wandering like that.'
else
mpecho $I says 'I'm nobody important. That's why I'm alive to answer you. Think about it.'
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog what huh lol lmao haha asdf blah qwerty gibberish~
if rand(25)
mpecho $I says 'I have no idea what that was, and I refuse to learn.'
else
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Was that a word? In this realm? Bold of you.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I stares at you the way you'd stare at a dog that started reciting poetry.
else
mpecho $I says 'Laugh all you want. The monsters down the road laugh too, and theirs is worse.'
endif
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog nice cool awesome love great amazing beautiful~
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Flattery. From a stranger covered in someone else's blood. How wholesome.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'Yes, I am wonderful. It changes nothing about your situation, but yes.'
else
mpecho $I almost smiles, catches itself, and returns to a professional scowl.
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog stupid idiot ugly suck noob dumb loser trash~
if rand(25)
mpecho $I says 'Says the hero who's been lost in the same three rooms for ten minutes.'
else
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Insults? From you? That's the bravest thing you've done all day, and it's a low bar.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'I've been called worse by better, and I outlived all of them. Care to apply?'
else
mpecho $I says 'Big words from a creature with a respawn timer.'
endif
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog mud game lag link bug immortal imm code reboot copyover~
if rand(25)
mpecho $I says 'The immortals built this place. They also broke it, fixed it, and broke it again. We don't ask.'
else
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'If the world freezes, that's not magic, that's lag. Stand very still and pray to the coders.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'Found a bug? Tell an immortal. They love that. They love it SO much.'
else
mpecho $I glances upward as if listening to something far above the sky, then shrugs it off.
endif
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog gold plat coin free give spare donate beg~
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Spare gold? Adventurer, you're carrying a sword worth more than my house.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'I don't give handouts. The monsters give handouts — handfuls, mostly your own.'
else
mpecho $I says 'You want free? Go to the newbie zones. Out here, everything bites back for payment.'
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog marry kiss date cute hot single~
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'I've outlived three spouses and a continent. Try someone with a shorter memory.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'Charming. The last person who flirted with me also tried to rob me. Funny coincidence.'
else
mpecho $I says 'No. But I admire the confidence of a person actively on fire asking me out.'
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog kill fight attack die murder destroy~
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Threaten me? I'm not even the scary thing in this room, and I'm definitely scarier than you.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'Go ahead. The guards are bored, the gods are watching, and I'm insured.'
else
mpecho $I says 'You want a fight? The whole realm is a fight. Walk twenty feet, it'll find you.'
endif
endif
~
|
